{
  "schema_version": "heel.host-ingress-runtime-lock.v1",
  "profile": "ingress-v1",
  "note": "Immutable inputs for scripts/host_ingress_proof.py. Every archive is fetched over HTTPS into private scratch and must match its SHA-256 before use. Hosted image, kernel and compiler/toolchain versions are recorded observations, not reproducible pins.",
  "notes": [
    "Total deadlines in policy.js (deadline()/settle(), H0BTD section 5.1) depend on pinned njs 1.0.2 (commit 72e6a980) internals, observed in its source: ngx_qjs_timer_handler deletes a timer's event after the callback returns, so clearTimeout() on a fired timer (from its callback or a microtask it runs) deletes it twice and kills the worker; the policy therefore never clears a fired timer.",
    "A timer callback that throws returns NGX_ERROR, which ngx_http_js_event_finalize turns into ngx_http_terminate_request (cleanups run, upstream closed, terminate handler posted); the zero-delay timer's own completion runs the posted requests, releasing the connection, its limit_conn slot and the JS context at the deadline.",
    "Any change to the nginx, njs or QuickJS pins must re-run the G8 deadline gates (dribble, boundary, late body, cap release, slow upstream, mixed load) and the G9 worker sentinel on the Linux proof job before review; macOS/kqueue results do not carry over to Linux/epoll.",
    "Host fingerprint normalisation (launcher, H0BL section 4): firewall state is read as `iptables-save` and `nft -s list ruleset` (stateless, no counter values). Before hashing, only the dated `# Generated by` and `# Completed on` lines are dropped from iptables-save output and its chain packet/byte counters `[n:m]` become `[-:-]`; any nft `counter packets n bytes m` becomes `counter`. Every table, chain name, policy and rule byte is kept. Two snapshots two seconds apart must agree before the namespace child starts, or the run fails closed with `fingerprint_unstable` and the unstable key names."
  ],
